<title>USA: Phoenix Duff Q4 shr profit vs pro forma loss.</title>
<headline>Phoenix Duff Q4 shr profit vs pro forma loss.</headline>
<dateline>HARTFORD, Conn. 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Phoenix Duff &amp; Phelps</p>
<p>			    Three Months Ended  Twelve Months Ended</p>
<p>			 Dec. 31,    Dec. 31,    Dec. 31,  Dec. 31,</p>
<p>				1996	 1995	  1996	1995</p>
<p>			 Actual Pro Forma(1)    Actual Pro Forma(1)</p>
<p>(in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p> Revenues		$36,264    $42,086    $152,504  $165,339</p>
<p> Net earnings	    6,684    (1,438)	26,719    17,967</p>
<p>Net income per common share</p>
<p>    Primary		 0.12    ( 0.06)	  0.50	0.30</p>
<p>    Fully diluted	 0.12	   --	  0.49	  --</p>
<p>Weighted average common shares</p>
<p>outstanding</p>
<p>     Primary	    44,327     44,010	44,215    43,963</p>
<p>     Fully diluted    54,180     53,812	54,093    53,798</p>
<p>NOTE (1): Phoenix Duff &amp; Phelps Corporation was formed Nov. 1, 1995, by a reverse merger involving Phoenix Securities Group, a subsidiary of Phoenix Home Life, and Duff &amp; Phelps Corporation.  In accordance with generally accepted accounting principles for this type of transaction, pro forma information has been presented for comparison on a post merger basis.</p>
